WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.050
In the 1950s and 60s, men from Gujarat and
Punjab came to Britain to work in mills

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.420
and factories.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.230
In 1972, Gujarati Hindus
expelled from Uganda arrived,

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.080
many with business skills.

5
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:18.440
Then came Tamil Hindus from
Sri Lanka, escaping civil war.

6
00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.970
Today, just over 1 million
Hindus live in England and Wales.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:28.450
So can a tradition this old live on in
a Leicester terrace or a London suburb?

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.870
In this mission, you'll follow the journey
from front-room shrines to purpose-built

9
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.910
mandirs.

10
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.010
Then you'll see where British
law and Hindu practice meet.

11
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: find out how Hindus keep
an ancient tradition alive in Britain.
